# Wiring proof for exec= argument splitting.
#
# The runner splits an exec= value the way a shell does: a quoted span stays ONE
# argv element. The fixture receives `one | two three` as a single argument and
# fails when it receives four, so a runner that splits on whitespace turns this
# test red. That is the defect this test pins: `ze cli -c "validate config
# bad.conf | json"` used to hand -c the word `"validate` and the rest of the
# pipeline as separate arguments.

option=timeout:value=20s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture runner/exec-quoted-argument "one | two three"
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=quoted-argument-intact
